[Music]  our minority rights in India under  threat in a country known for pluralism  India's secularists face their biggest  challenge yet vigilante attacks on  Muslims have shocked many Indians a  firebrand Hindu cleric with a published  private militia now runs India's largest  state on social media and TV Hindu  culture warriors promote hardline  identity politics  India's ruling Bharatiya janta party  bears some of the blame for this new  extremism but there's also something  deeper going on simply put the model of  Indian secularism has failed tip toeing  around religious sensitivities India led  different religions implement their own  personal laws rather than have one law  for all this meant customs like polygamy  or divorce by decree are legal for  Muslims but not for Christians or Hindus  championing group rights over individual  rights and tolerating regressive  religious practices bred Hindu  resentment Indian secularists are right  to worry about a new wave of bigotry but  to fight it they need to look forward  not backward rather than go back to a  failed model that prioritized special  rights for some they should champion  equal rights for all to learn more about  my take on India check the links in the  description below also let us know what  other topics you want our scholars to  cover in 60 seconds and be sure to  subscribe for more research and videos  from AEI

